quiz:
Let's check the attention we've covered so far with a quiz.

```quiz
{
  "title": "Attention check quiz",
  "questions": [
    { "type": "ox", "question": "An attention score is computed from the dot product of a Query and a Key.", "answer": true, "explanation": "The **dot product** of the Query with each Key becomes the relevance score, and softmax turns it into weights." },
    { "type": "choice", "question": "Why do we divide the scores by $\\sqrt{d_k}$?", "choices": ["To make the computation faster", "To keep the dot product from growing so large that softmax collapses onto one entry", "To match the size of the Value vectors", "To normalize the Keys"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "When the dimension is large, the variance of the dot product grows and the softmax gradient becomes nearly zero. Dividing rescales the magnitude." },
    { "type": "short", "question": "What is the name of the vectors that the attention weights are used to take a weighted sum of?", "answer": "Value", "accept": ["V", "values"], "explanation": "The weights are multiplied with the **Value** vectors to form the new representation." }
  ]
}
```

